New partial, following `_notification-list.scss` verbatim as the idiom — first line `@use "../../../../node_modules/govuk-frontend" as *;`.

```
.app-commodity-total {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  padding: govuk-spacing(4);
  background-color: govuk-colour("light-grey");

  &__value {
    @include govuk-font($size: 48, $weight: bold);
    margin-bottom: govuk-spacing(1);
    color: govuk-colour("blue");
  }

  &__label {
    @include govuk-font($size: 24, $weight: bold);
    margin-bottom: govuk-spacing(2);
    color: govuk-colour("blue");
  }

  &__caption {
    @include govuk-font($size: 19);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: $govuk-text-colour;
  }
}
```

No raw hex values, no bespoke font sizes, no media queries — `govuk-grid-column-one-half` already goes full width below tablet, so the cards stack for free. Do NOT use `$app-light-grey` (#f8f8f8): it is the wrong token. Must pass `npm run lint:scss` (stylelint-config-gds/scss). No comments in the file.
